---
# The homepage is titled after the site, whatever the site is called: the
# base layout then emits <title> as the bare site name instead of doubling it.
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ site.name }}"
titleScreenReaderOnly: true
layout: layouts/pagealign.liquid
eleventyImport:
  collections: ["post"]
---
{%- comment %} Structured after the port source's own index.liquid: an intro
   block, then curated sections of a few posts each, each ending in a link to
   the fuller list — not a flat dump of every post.

   The source has two sections, "Newest" and "Popular". Popular is not ported:
   it reads collections.popularPostsRanked, which _11ty/analyticsPlugin.js
   builds from a committed JSON of his page views. An Indiekit site has no
   equivalent data source, and inventing a ranking would be fiction. Newest is
   the section that carries over; the archive holds everything.
   {% endcomment -%}
<div class="about-description">
	<p>{{ site.description }}</p>
</div>

<h2>Newest</h2>
<ol class="posts h-feed">
{%- comment %} reverse THEN limit. LiquidJS applies `limit` before `reversed`,
   so `collections.post reversed limit: 5` takes the five OLDEST posts and
   reverses those — not the five newest. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign recentPosts = collections.post | reverse -%}
{%- for post in recentPosts limit: 5 %}
  {%- comment %} The social counts, and the post-type icon, are captured HERE,
     before the `page: post` override below, on purpose. @11ty/font-awesome
     registers each icon's sprite symbol against `this.page.url` (plugin.js:51).
     Rendered inside the override, every {{ "{% icon %}" }} filed its symbol under the
     POST's url while the listing page emitted a <use href="#..."> for a symbol
     that was never in its own bundle — the icon painted nothing. Capturing
     outside the override files the symbol against this listing page, where
     {{ "{% getBundle %}" }} outputs it. The override itself stays: date filters must
     read each post's own front matter (see post-list-entry.liquid). {% endcomment -%}
  {%- capture socialHtml %}{% include "partials/post-social-counts.liquid", post: post %}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- capture postTypeIconHtml %}{% include "partials/post-type-icon.liquid", post: post %}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- include "partials/post-list-entry.liquid", post: post, page: post, socialHtml: socialHtml, postTypeIconHtml: postTypeIconHtml -%}
{%- endfor %}
	<li><em><a href="/archive/" class="posts-link posts-link-more">…see the full archive.</a></em></li>
</ol>
